# IMPORTANT CHANGE TO THE OLD MAX_WORKERS=1 RULE

The previous `MAX_WORKERS=1` decision was created because the historical worker benchmark showed a 36% pass rate and additional parallelism would simply multiply bad work.

Do NOT blindly interpret “three FreeLLMAPI models available” as permission to run three coding workers simultaneously.

Use three providers/routes as **resilience capacity first**.

Initially:

`MAX_ACTIVE_IMPLEMENTATION_WORKERS = 1`

The other FreeLLMAPI routes are available for failover/retry.

Only increase concurrent implementation workers after the representative visual/Android benchmark demonstrates the previously agreed ≥60% pass threshold and the tasks are demonstrably independent.

At that point, up to three independent workers may run concurrently if:

* their file ownership does not overlap;
* their WorkItems do not depend on each other;
* each has its own worktree;
* integration remains serialized;
* acceptance remains independent.

This preserves the lessons from the previous orchestration failure while still making use of the three available worker routes.

