---

# WATCHDOG MUST NOT CREATE SUPERVISOR SPRAWL

The watchdog is not another planner.

It must not repeatedly create:

supervisor → supervisor → supervisor → worker

chains.

Its job is mechanical recovery.

The correct pattern is:

Director dies
→ durable state remains
→ new director session reads state
→ continue

Worker dies
→ lease expires
→ controller returns task to recoverable state
→ new worker attempts it

Provider rate-limits
→ attempt records infrastructure failure
→ alternate provider/cooldown
→ continue later

Reviewer unavailable
→ review remains pending
→ capacity returns
→ fresh reviewer consumes durable review packet

This is recovery, not recursive orchestration.

